<title>SINGAPORE: Thai Bangchak issues tender to buy March crude.</title>
<headline>Thai Bangchak issues tender to buy March crude.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangchak Petroleum Plc has issued a tender to buy 500,000 barrels of Middle East and 600,000 barrels of Far East crude oils, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on Wednesday and is valid for 24 hours, the sources said.</p>
<p>The refiner traditionally seeks Oman, Dubai or similar crude grades from the Middle East. It has awarded Iranian heavy in its last two monthly tenders.</p>
<p>It also seeks light sweet regional grades, such as Tapis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
